message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived Zenodo release using the
  metadata below and cite the associated manuscript when available.
title: "Analysis code for single-nucleus multiomic profiling of Parkinson's disease midbrain"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Mingming
    affiliation: Yale University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7357-0272"
date-released: 2026-08-13
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21924320"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21924320"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheDongLab/PD-Midbrain-Multiome"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for single-nucleus RNA and chromatin-accessibility profiling
  of postmortem human midbrain samples spanning healthy controls, incidental
  Lewy body disease, and Parkinson's disease. The repository contains R,
  Python, and shell scripts for multiome processing, QTL and GWAS integration,
  differential expression, peak-gene linking, and regulatory-network analyses.
keywords:
  - Parkinson's disease
  - single-nucleus multiome
  - snRNA-seq
  - snATAC-seq
  - chromatin accessibility
  - gene regulation
  - QTL
